        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe unused-export baseline still treated seven private policy implementation details as public module surface.\n\nRelated: #105595\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nMake five policy evidence scanners and two fix-metadata declarations module-private. Tests now exercise scanner behavior through the supported `collectPolicyEvidence` aggregate while retaining direct coverage of the public metadata lookup.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime behavior change. The shrink-only dead-code baseline drops to 3,299 entries at the pushed head.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/check-deadcode-exports.mjs --update`\n- `node scripts/check-deadcode-exports.mjs`\n- `pnpm deadcode:dependencies`\n- `pnpm format:check` on touched files\n- `git diff --check`\n- Policy Testbox: 6 files, 344 tests passed: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29242972968\n- Fresh autoreview: no accepted/actionable findings\n",
